infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Transcode up front vs on demand
  desc One source becomes a rendition ladder — pay storage + compute now, or stall the first viewer later
  compares
    - label Transcode everything up front
      children
        - label Instant playback at any rendition
          desc Every 240p…4K shard is already in object storage
        - label More storage + compute per upload
          desc You pay the full ladder bill on every video, even unpopular ones
        - label Best for popular formats
          desc Large platforms pre-transcode the common codecs eagerly
    - label Transcode on demand
      children
        - label Cheaper storage
          desc Rare renditions are never generated until requested
        - label First viewer stalls on a cold rendition
          desc The cold path must encode before playback can start
        - label Best for the long tail
          desc Lazily generate rare formats only when someone asks
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f59e0b
